    "overview": "Flarepost is a working sheet for mail. A separate navigation plane frames the reading surface, and tonal surfaces and spacing make a busy list easy to scan. The existing Flarepost fold mark from `public/brand/` anchors the identity.\n\nLight mode pairs a charcoal navigation plane with a trace of violet and a near-white workspace. In the workspace, muted violet marks branding, primary actions, links, and focus. Hover, selection, and unread states use shades of gray. Dark mode uses neutral graphite surfaces and reserves muted lavender for branding, actions, focus, and fine state markers. Use familiar controls and let weight, alignment and spacing do most of the work. Carry the same visual grammar through full width and narrow layouts, with equal care for both.",
